    "structural_proof": "Every 7-vertex unit-distance graph is 4-colourable. By OEIS A186705 the maximum numbers of unit distances on 7,6,5,4,3 points are 12,9,7,5,3, so every induced subgraph has minimum degree at most 3: the graph is 3-degenerate. A proper 4-colouring splits into at most five independent classes of size <=2 (split classes into pairs), and no class of size <=2 contains a 3-vertex monochromatic pattern. Hence no 7-vertex unit-distance graph can force a monochromatic sqrt(3)-triangle at k=5.",
